{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in, you're grand. What has you here today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Back.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Low down, or up at the shoulders?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Low.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long, and what started it?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Overdone it.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Err, three weeks, doctor, since she was lifting boxes in work. The low back shoots down the left leg. Worse when she sits, and walking eases it a small bit.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Three weeks of low back pain after the boxes, shooting down the left leg, worse with sitting, easier when you walk. Have I that right?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Umm. The leg itself, how does it feel?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Feet feel dead.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Feet feel dead. Both feet?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Both.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): And your energy?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Wet rag.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Like a wet rag, tired so. Does the leg give way?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any trouble passing water, or numbness where you sit?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): No waterworks trouble, no saddle numbness. Hot or shivery?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She was raging about the waiting room.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Can't hear myself think.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): That'll be the radio. I won't record it. What pain relief are you on?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Ibuprofin.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ibuprofen. Dose, and how often?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The ibuprofen, four hundred milligrams, three times a day, by mouth, the whole three weeks, for the back.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ibuprofen four hundred milligrams three times daily by mouth for the back. Exercises?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Your man Declan at her work has her doing knees-to-chest stretches morning and night.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any use?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): No use in them. The nurse left this card. I nearly took the pressure as one sixteen over seventy-seven, but today it is one oh nine over seventy-seven.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Temperature thirty-eight point three. And the weight, I had fifty-four, no, the slip says fifty-two kilos.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Last time in March you were sixty-eight. Your last pressure was one-forty.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Old figures, leave them. A small bit warm on the reading, though you don't feel hot. Couch, please.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Straight leg, the left one. When it catches, say.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Now.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Positive straight leg raise on the left, pain at about forty degrees.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right side is clear, full lift, no pain. Low lumbar midline tender, no spasm.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Working impression is sciatica, nerve root irritation. Provisional.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll refer you to physio.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): We might do a scan if it does not settle.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): Stay with the ibuprofen and food, keep moving, break up the sitting. Sooner if you cannot pass water or the leg gives way.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let's see you in two weeks.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'll see she gets to the physio.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mind how you go."
 ],
